From: Seyoon Ragavan <complexzetaprime@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:23:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] NP's closure moves to PClosure as preimage_mem_NP; TMSAT's
 prefix-extraction step no longer depends on the simp set

Reductions returns to the campaign's text: its import of PClosure brought Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith
into its downstream modules, which made Mathlib's simp lemma Nat.cast_min reshape a goal in
TMSAT's tmsat_take_computes. The theorem now lives beside preimage_mem_P, stated for preimages
(NP is closed under polynomial-time preimages, so under Karp reductions), with no new import.
TMSAT's step replaces min a.length b.length by its value in each case before simp, so no min is
left to reshape; it holds with and without Linarith in scope. tmsat_take_computes gains its proof
sketch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
